# READ-FIELD-CLOSURE (Codex K03-READ-FIELD-CLOSURE-20261008-31, -29 step 3): aliases through a merge result.  h, a
# root merge result, is held in its statement's output place; Model's code reads node\h\p twice and node\h\q.
# b's copy of the unit holds h's place -- the edge chain through that statement, then h, an actual Structure,
# whole past the crossing -- and neither the statement's code (h's merge frame) nor Hold, its operand: the use
# named the statement's slot alone before, and the copy took the statement whole.  Exit 7.
Hold:
    int: p 3
    int: q 4
    int: r 5
end: Hold
h: merge: Hold
Model:
    int: k 0
    k: node\h\p + node\h\p + node\h\q
end: Model
b: merge: Model
b
int: ok 7
if: b\k != 10
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
